/* book exam traps: Do not say a magneto needs a battery. A magneto makes its own primary current from a rotating magnet. | Primary current, about 4 A, is not the spark current. The secondary sends a short high-voltage pulse at low current. | The contact breaker interrupts the primary circuit, not the secondary. The secondary voltage appears because the primary field collapses. | A distributor does not make the spark. It routes the coil's high voltage to the correct plug. | The condenser is not only a radio filter. It reduces point arcing and helps the primary current fall fast. */
