/* book: lead: Electronic ignition replaces the contact breaker, the part that burns, wears and drifts out of time, with a sensor and a power transistor or thyristor. The spark becomes stronger at high speed, the timing stays set for the life of the engine, and an ECU can choose the spark angle for every speed and load. Laser ignition goes one step further and removes the spark plug's electrodes altogether, igni */
/* book Figure 2.10.1: Top: in breakerless ignition a Hall trigger tells the module when to switch the coil, so no points wear. Bottom: in laser ignition the second worked example’s 30 mJ, 6 ns pulse is focused through a window to a 50 μm spot, where 2.5×10¹¹ W/cm² breaks the gas down into a plasma that lights the charge. */
