/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In transistor-assisted contact (TAC) ignition the points stay, but they carry only the small base current of a power transistor, and the transistor switches the coil current.
   - A breakerless (transistorised) system removes the points.
   - The module also controls dwell.
   - With an ECU the distributor can go too.
   - Capacitor discharge ignition (CDI) stores energy in a capacitor instead of the coil.
   - E is the energy stored in the capacitor (J); C is its capacitance (F); V is the charging voltage (V).
   - In laser ignition a short pulse from a laser, typically a nanosecond-pulse solid-state laser, passes through a window in the head and is focused by a lens to a tiny spot inside the charge.
*/
