/* book Worked example: Q: A CDI unit charges a 1 μF capacitor to 400 V. Find the stored energy per spark, compare it with the 29 mJ that a points coil delivers at 6000 rpm, and find the average power the charger must supply to a four-cylinder four-stroke engine at 6000 rpm.
   1. E = ½ C V² = 0.5 × 1×10⁻⁶ × 400² = 0.5 × 1×10⁻⁶ × 160 000 = 0.080 J = 80 mJ.
   2. 80 ÷ 29 = 2.8, so the CDI stores almost three times the energy of the points coil at that speed.
   3. Sparks per second: each cylinder fires once every two revolutions, so 4 × 6000 ÷ 2 ÷ 60 = 200 sparks/s.
   4. Average power = 200 × 0.080 = 16 W.
   Answer: 80 mJ per spark, about 2.8 times the inductive coil at 6000 rpm, and an average charging power of 16 W. */
