/* book Worked example 2: Q: A laser gives 30 mJ pulses lasting 6 ns, focused to a spot 50 μm in diameter. Find the peak power and the intensity at the focus in W/cm².
   1. Peak power = energy ÷ time = 0.030 ÷ (6×10⁻⁹) = 5×10⁶ W = 5 MW.
   2. Spot radius = 25 μm = 25×10⁻⁴ cm; area = π × (25×10⁻⁴)² = 1.963×10⁻⁵ cm².
   3. Intensity = 5×10⁶ ÷ 1.963×10⁻⁵ = 2.55×10¹¹ W/cm².
   Answer: 5 MW peak and about 2.5×10¹¹ W/cm², in the range where air breaks down; the same 30 mJ spread over 1 ms would give only 30 W. */
