/* book exam traps: Electronic ignition still uses an ignition coil; what it removes is the contact breaker. Only CDI moves the energy store from the coil to a capacitor. | Wasted spark is not a misfire. The second spark at the end of the exhaust stroke meets no fresh charge and does no harm. | CDI gives a fast, strong but short spark; do not write that it is better in every way. A long inductive spark is better for lean mixtures. | In laser ignition the laser does not heat the whole charge; it breaks down a tiny volume at the focus, and a normal flame does the rest. | Peak laser power is energy ÷ pulse time, not energy × time; with a 6 ns pulse a few millijoules give megawatts. */
